@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: Self Provisioning
	Testing the Self Provisioning portlet.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| SFPZENSFPZEN |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| SFPZENSFPZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View dxp options
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	DXP activation key options should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | SFPZENSFPZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	Then the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.4                           |
	| Version | 7.3                           |
	| Version | 7.2                           |
	| Version | 7.1                           |
	| Version | 7.0                           |

Scenario: View portal options
	Portal activation key options should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | SFPZENSFPZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	Then the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Portal"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | Portal                        |
	| Version | 6.2                           |
	| Version | 6.1                           |
	| Version | 6.0                           |
	| Version | 5.2                           |
	| Version | 5.1                           |

Scenario: View commerce options
	Commerce activation key options should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | SFPZENSFPZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce Subscription Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 0 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	Then the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Liferay Commerce"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | Commerce Subscription         |
	| Version | 1                             |

Scenario: View employee options
	Appropriate activation key options should be visible according to the permissions that employees have.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "sfp.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Liferay, Inc.         |
	| Product | Commerce Subscription |
	| Product | DXP                   |
	| Product | Portal                |

Scenario: Download dxp self provisioning license
	DXP activation key should be downloaded according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | SFPZENSFPZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	Then the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	And I download a Self Provisioning license with the following options
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.4                           |
	And I download a Self Provisioning license with the following options
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.3                           |
	And I download a Self Provisioning license with the following options
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.2                           |
	And I download a Self Provisioning license with the following options
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.1                           |
	And I download a Self Provisioning license with the following options
	| Project | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.0                           |
	Then I should be able to view the downloaded "xml" license file the with the following parameters
	| License Type | activation-key            |
	| Product      | DXP Development           |
	| Version      | 7.4                       |
	| License Name | Developer Activation Keys |
	And I should be able to view the downloaded "xml" license file the with the following parameters
	| License Type | activation-key            |
	| Product      | DXP Development           |
	| Version      | 7.3                       |
	| License Name | Developer Activation Keys |
	And I should be able to view the downloaded "xml" license file the with the following parameters
	| License Type | activation-key            |
	| Product      | DXP Development           |
	| Version      | 7.1                       |
	| License Name | Developer Activation Keys |
	And I should be able to view the downloaded "xml" license file the with the following parameters
	| License Type | activation-key            |
	| Product      | DXP Development           |
	| Version      | 7.0                       |
	| License Name | Developer Activation Keys |

Scenario: View commerce options via commerce for dxp cloud purchase
	View commerce options when there is an active commerce for dxp cloud subscription on their account.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sfp.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SFP                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | SFPZENSFPZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sfp.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Sfpzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce for DXP Cloud Production" on koroneiki with the following values
